        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-24T12:54:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I think so. Actually this page fault handler can be also called from kvm_vcpu_pre_fault_memory() which is triggered by userspace, but kvm_vcpu_pre_fault_memory() itself loads the vCPU before doing that, so that should be also fine.\n\nSo yeah, I hope 4 arguments will be enough in v6.15.\n\nBTW the difference of this vm_mmu_map is that other for PV interfaces we switch to the guest VMCS and then back to the host VMCS (in .switch_to_guest_vcpu() and .switch_to_host_vcpu()) while in vm_mmu_map we don\u0027t need to. I hope that won\u0027t be a problem.",
      "parentUuid": "7c37eeec_fb17e4e9",
      "revId": "bec247fb33d7e8d01356cea19ad8f513fcd15dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
